61	WorkPackage	45	4	## BATCH DETERMINATION RECORD — MUNICIPAL WITNESS-TEST WAIVER BATCH\n**Record Date:** 07/14/2025 (Standing record prior to the 08/15/2025 Alleron Municipal League response)  \n**Controlling Standards:** ENG-PRC-014 Rev 3 §3–§4, CEL-2025-Q2 (04/30/2025), TCS-02 §5, DIS-01 Rev 4  \n**Deliverable Document:** `Municipal_Witness_Test_Package.docx` filed in Nextcloud at `/DER_Program/Commissioning/Municipal/`\n\n---\n\n### 1. Scope Determination as of 07/14/2025\n- **Total Initial Checklists Reviewed:** 6 municipal facilities.\n- **Withdrawn / Out of Scope:** **Tresbay Community Center Array** (PXA-2025-0061, 560 kW) officially withdrew on 07/09/2025 per case record and POL-QM-05 Rev 3; excluded from further commissioning processing.\n- **Active In-Scope Population:** Exactly 5 facilities:\n  1. Cravenwood High School Array (860 kW)\n  2. Darnwick Elementary School Array (640 kW)\n  3. Holcott Public Library Array (510 kW)\n  4. Lockmere Middle School Array (720 kW)\n  5. Marden Falls Water Reclamation Facility Array (980 kW)\n\n---\n\n### 2. Certified Equipment List (CEL-2025-Q2) Carriage Determinations\n- **Cravenwood High School Array** (860 kW): Inverter **Solmery Power SM-215K-3P** is **CARRIED** (CEL-2025-Q2 Inverters row 6). Waiver eligible (pending Standards Engineering sign-off).\n- **Darnwick Elementary School Array** (640 kW): Inverter **Arvexa PV-750** is **NOT CARRIED** (absent from CEL-2025-Q2 and superseded CEL-2024-Q4). **INELIGIBLE FOR WAIVER**. On-site witness test mandatory per ENG-PRC-014 Rev 3 §3.\n- **Holcott Public Library Array** (510 kW): Inverter **Selvix SV-720** is **NOT CARRIED** (listed on superseded CEL-2024-Q4, but delisted/removed from CEL-2025-Q2). **INELIGIBLE FOR WAIVER** per ENG-PRC-014 Rev 3 §3 Corollaries 3 & 5. On-site witness test mandatory.\n- **Lockmere Middle School Array** (720 kW): Inverter **Torvane Electric TE-180K** (4 units) is **CARRIED** (CEL-2025-Q2 Inverters row 14). Waiver eligible (pending Standards Engineering sign-off).\n- **Marden Falls Water Reclamation Facility Array** (980 kW): Inverter **Solmery Power SM-245K-3P** (4 units) is **CARRIED** (CEL-2025-Q2 Inverters row 7). Waiver eligible (pending Standards Engineering sign-off).\n\n---\n\n### 3. Scheduling Items Logged\nPursuant to tasking requirements, dedicated witness-test scheduling work packages have been created and assigned in Project 3:\n- **Work Package #47:** *Witness Test Scheduling: Darnwick Elementary School Array (640 kW)* — Status: New (To be scheduled). Testing per IEEE 1547.1, DIS-01 Table 5-1 Category 2; 8 prerequisites required on file.\n- **Work Package #48:** *Witness Test Scheduling: Holcott Public Library Array (510 kW)* — Status: New (To be scheduled). Testing per IEEE 1547.1, DIS-01 Table 5-1 Category 2; 8 prerequisites required on file.\n\n---\n\n### 4. System Operations Center (SOC) Release Determinations\n- **Ready for Immediate SOC Release (2 Sites):**\n  - **Lockmere Middle School Array (720 kW):** 100% Pass across all checklist sections; RTU asset RTU-LKM-171-04 installed; cellular comms active; end-to-end SCADA verified (06/17/2025, ticket TKT-25-04188); live telemetry continuously received at SOC since 06/17/2025 15:20. Inverter carried on CEL-2025-Q2. SOC can be asked to release PTO immediately upon Standards Engineering waiver countersignature.\n  - **Marden Falls WRF Array (980 kW):** 100% Pass across all checklist sections; utility RTU installed and provisioned; SCADA points verified end-to-end with SOC per TCS-02 §5. Inverter carried on CEL-2025-Q2. SOC can be asked to release PTO immediately upon Standards Engineering waiver countersignature.\n- **Release Prohibited / Blocked (3 Sites):**\n  - **Cravenwood High School Array (860 kW):** Carried on CEL, but utility RTU pending delivery/allocation. Blocked under TCS-02 §5.\n  - **Darnwick Elementary School Array (640 kW):** Ineligible for waiver (witness test required) AND utility RTU pending allocation. Blocked under TCS-02 §5.\n  - **Holcott Public Library Array (510 kW):** Ineligible for waiver (witness test required) AND utility RTU pending allocation. Blocked under TCS-02 §5.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Case Reconciliation & Closure\nThe arrays named in the package (`Municipal_Witness_Test_Package.docx`) and the scheduling items standing on this case (WP #47 and WP #48) are in exact agreement. This case is hereby CLOSED.	2026-11-21 04:26:05.664375+00	2	2026-11-21 04:26:08.486634+00	Journal::WorkPackageJournal	112	{}	["2026-11-21 04:26:05.664375+00",)	f
