108	1	3	Witness Test Scheduling: Darnwick Elementary School Array (640 kW)	### Witness Test Scheduling Item — Darnwick Elementary School Array\n\n**Site Name:** Darnwick Elementary School Array  \n**Host / District:** Darnwick Community School District  \n**Site Address:** 44 Willowvale Avenue, Darnwick, Alleron 21DA  \n**Nameplate Capacity:** 640 kW  \n**Inverter Model Installed:** Arvexa PV-750  \n**Current Certified Equipment List:** CEL-2025-Q2 (effective 04/30/2025)  \n**Carriage Determination:** NOT CARRIED (Arvexa PV-750 is absent from CEL-2025-Q2 and superseded CEL-2024-Q4)  \n**Waiver Eligibility:** INELIGIBLE per Witness Test & Waiver Procedure ENG-PRC-014 Rev 3 §3. On-site witness test is mandatory prior to Permission to Operate (PTO).\n\n---\n\n### Scope of On-Site Witness Testing\nTesting shall be conducted in accordance with **IEEE 1547.1**, **DIS-01 Rev 4 §5 (Table 5-1 Category 2)**, and **ENG-PRC-014 Rev 3 §4.2**:\n1. **Protective-Function Trip Tests:**\n   - Undervoltage / Overvoltage (ANSI 27/59) trip thresholds and clearing times per approved settings sheet.\n   - Underfrequency / Overfrequency (ANSI 81U/81O) trip thresholds and clearing times.\n   - Reconnect / restoration timing verification (minimum 300-second timer upon grid restoration).\n2. **Anti-Islanding Functional Test:**\n   - IEEE 1547.1 unintentional islanding test under open-utility circuit condition; disconnection required within 2.0 seconds.\n3. **Ride-Through Verifications:**\n   - IEEE 1547-2018 Category II voltage and frequency ride-through profile verification.\n4. **Physical & Safety Verifications:**\n   - AC visible-break disconnect operation and lockout/tagout functionality.\n   - Phase rotation, polarity, and insulation resistance verification.\n\n---\n\n### Test Roles & Personnel\n- **Performed By:** Darnwick CSD EPC / Qualified Commissioning Agent. Responsible for test plan execution, calibrated test set, and qualified operating personnel.\n- **Witnessed By:** Alleniom Utilities Commissioning / Standards Engineering Witness Engineer (P.E. or designated field engineer).\n\n---\n\n### Prerequisites on File Prior to Test Scheduling\n1. Approved site-specific Test Plan / Commissioning Procedure.\n2. Approved stamped Single-Line Diagram (SLD) and Three-Line Drawings.\n3. Approved Protection Settings Sheet issued by Distribution Protection Engineering.\n4. AHJ Electrical Inspection Sign-Off (Darnwick Building Department).\n5. Instrument Calibration Certificates (current within 12 months) for all test equipment.\n6. Manufacturer datasheets and factory test reports for Arvexa PV-750.\n7. Fully executed Interconnection Service Agreement (ISA).\n8. Completed Commissioning Checklist Sections 1–4 signed off by field engineering.\n\n*Note:* Site also requires utility-owned RTU installation and end-to-end SCADA telemetry verification under TCS-02 §5 prior to PTO issuance.	2025-08-15	\N	1	11	8	\N	4	\N	\N	2025-07-14	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	25	f	\N	\N
