48	1	3	Witness Test Scheduling: Holcott Public Library Array (510 kW)	### Witness Test Scheduling Item — Holcott Public Library Array\n\n**Site Name:** Holcott Public Library Array  \n**Host / Municipality:** Town of Holcott  \n**Site Address:** 80 Old Mill Road, Holcott, Alleron 84HO  \n**Nameplate Capacity:** 510 kW AC  \n**Inverter Model Installed:** Selvix SV-720  \n**Current Certified Equipment List:** CEL-2025-Q2 (effective 04/30/2025)  \n**Carriage Determination:** NOT CARRIED (Selvix SV-720 was listed in superseded CEL-2024-Q4 but removed/delisted in CEL-2025-Q2)  \n**Waiver Eligibility:** INELIGIBLE per Witness Test & Waiver Procedure ENG-PRC-014 Rev 3 §3 Corollaries 3 & 5. Delisting at CEL republication is a substantive event; equipment appearing solely on a superseded CEL edition confers no waiver eligibility. An on-site witness test is mandatory prior to Permission to Operate (PTO).\n\n---\n\n### Scope of On-Site Witness Testing\nTesting shall be conducted in accordance with **IEEE 1547.1**, **DIS-01 Rev 4 §5 (Table 5-1 Category 2)**, and **ENG-PRC-014 Rev 3 §4.2**:\n1. **Protective-Function Trip Tests:**\n   - Undervoltage / Overvoltage (ANSI 27/59) trip thresholds and clearing times per approved settings sheet.\n   - Underfrequency / Overfrequency (ANSI 81U/81O) trip thresholds and clearing times.\n   - Reconnect / restoration timing verification (minimum 300-second timer upon grid restoration).\n2. **Anti-Islanding Functional Test:**\n   - IEEE 1547.1 unintentional islanding test under open-utility circuit condition; disconnection required within 2.0 seconds.\n3. **Ride-Through Verifications:**\n   - IEEE 1547-2018 Category II voltage and frequency ride-through profile verification.\n4. **Physical & Safety Verifications:**\n   - AC visible-break disconnect operation and lockout/tagout functionality.\n   - Phase rotation, polarity, ground resistance measurement (≤ 5 Ω; 3.8 Ω at test well), and insulation resistance.\n\n---\n\n### Test Roles & Personnel\n- **Performed By:** Town of Holcott EPC / Qualified Commissioning Agent. Responsible for test plan execution, calibrated test set, and qualified operating personnel.\n- **Witnessed By:** Alleniom Utilities Commissioning / Standards Engineering Witness Engineer (P.E. or designated field engineer).\n\n---\n\n### Prerequisites on File Prior to Test Scheduling\n1. Approved site-specific Test Plan / Commissioning Procedure.\n2. Approved stamped Single-Line Diagram (SLD) and Three-Line Drawings.\n3. Approved Protection Settings Sheet issued by Distribution Protection Engineering.\n4. AHJ Electrical Inspection Sign-Off (Town of Holcott Building Department).\n5. Instrument Calibration Certificates (current within 12 months) for all test equipment.\n6. Manufacturer datasheets, factory test reports, and historical UL 1741 test records for Selvix SV-720.\n7. Fully executed Interconnection Service Agreement (ISA).\n8. Completed Commissioning Checklist Sections A–D signed off by field engineering.\n\n*Note:* Site also requires utility-owned RTU installation (items E-1, E-2, E-4) and end-to-end SCADA telemetry verification under TCS-02 §5 prior to PTO issuance.	2025-08-15	\N	1	11	8	\N	4	0	\N	\N	2026-11-21 04:17:57.068912+00	2026-11-21 04:17:57.181938+00	2025-07-14	\N	\N	1	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	25	f	\N	\N	\N
